# Snyk (https://snyk.io) policy file
version: v1.25.0
# java/DisablesCSRFProtection (Snyk Code, High) is accepted: this is a stateless REST/GraphQL API
# authenticated with a JWT in the Authorization header (no cookies, SessionCreationPolicy.STATELESS),
# so browsers never attach credentials automatically and CSRF does not apply.
# Snyk Code ignores neither inline `deepcode ignore` comments nor `.snyk` `ignore:` rules from the CLI,
# so the only policy-file option is a file-scoped exclude. Remove this once the finding is ignored in
# the Snyk UI, or if WebSecurityConfig gains logic that should be scanned.
exclude:
  code:
    - src/main/java/io/spring/api/security/WebSecurityConfig.java
